<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <groupId>com.coobi.logistics</groupId>
  <artifactId>coobi-logistics</artifactId>
  <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>

  <name>coobi-logistics</name>
  <description>
    Aggregator of the three services of the Coobi Logistics pipeline: the telemetry
    simulator, the Kafka Streams processor and the read API.
  </description>

  <!--
    This project only aggregates; it is not the parent of the services, and it carries no
    configuration of its own. Every service keeps spring-boot-starter-parent as its
    parent, its own `mvnw`, and its own dependency set, so `mvn -f services/<service>/pom.xml
    test` keeps working exactly as it did before and nothing here can change what a service
    builds.

    It exists for the two things that cannot be expressed inside one service:

    * MVP-9.4, the full pipeline smoke test, lives in logistics-api and starts the stream
      processor in-process, so it needs the processor on its test classpath. Within one
      reactor build Maven resolves that dependency from `target/classes` of the processor
      module, which is what makes the test work without installing an executable (Spring
      Boot repackaged) artifact that cannot be used as a library.
    * one command that runs every unit suite and, with `-Dintegration-tests`, every
      container-backed integration test of the pipeline.
  -->
  <modules>
    <module>services/event-generator</module>
    <module>services/stream-processor</module>
    <module>services/logistics-api</module>
  </modules>
</project>
